{"id": "EUVD-2026-105084", "enisaUuid": "5961b6ac-9ae3-3b23-9d7a-85c45c2f940f", "description": "Stirling-PDF 3.0.0 through 3.2.0 contains an authorization bypass vulnerability that allows authenticated users to access other users' stored files by pointing a processing folder at the server storage directory. Attackers can create a folder via POST /api/v1/processing-folders targeting storage/<victimUserId>, list files, and run pipelines to read, modify, or destroy victims' files.", "datePublished": "2026-10-20T15:40:32", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-23T01:46:06", "baseScore": 7.1, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:L/VI:H/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/abraxas/stirling-storage-folder-idor", "https://abraxaslabs.tech/research/stirling-storage-folder-idor", "https://abraxaslabs.tech/research/stirling-pdf-3.2.0-leftovers", "https://github.com/Stirling-Tools/Stirling-PDF/blob/v3.2.0/app/proprietary/src/main/java/stirling/software/proprietary/policy/config/FolderAccessGuard.java", "https://github.com/Stirling-Tools/Stirling-PDF/blob/v3.2.0/app/proprietary/src/main/java/stirling/software/proprietary/policy/controller/ProcessingFolderController.java", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/stirling-pdf-3.0.0-through-3.2.0-authorization-bypass-via-processing-folders"], "aliases": ["GHSA-c89m-ff4c-f99w", "CVE-2026-113606"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.3, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "9be6bf1e-c596-30b8-9c32-3f51dc210225", "product": {"name": "Stirling-PDF", "vendor": {"name": "Stirling-Tools"}}, "product_version": "3.0.0 \u22643.2.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "92a001b1-6204-3988-9787-7a5ae5e79681", "vendor": {"name": "Stirling-Tools"}}], "isExploited": false}